1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,186
There is a piece of your brain that sits outside your skull, and you are using it right now.

2
00:00:07,186 --> 00:00:11,314
The retina is not an organ attached to the brain.

3
00:00:11,314 --> 00:00:17,789
It grows out of the brain while you are an embryo and stays brain tissue for life.

4
00:00:17,789 --> 00:00:27,963
Near its centre is a spot one and a half millimetres across called the macula, and that patch does almost all of your detailed vision.

5
00:00:27,963 --> 00:00:34,440
Every word you read happens there. Now here is the problem with that spot.

6
00:00:34,440 --> 00:00:41,626
The macula is the most light exposed tissue in your body, and one of the most oxygen hungry.

7
00:00:41,626 --> 00:00:52,086
Add a dense layer of fatty membranes that oxidise easily. If you were designing a tissue to be damaged, you would design this one.

8
00:00:52,086 --> 00:00:55,716
So your body puts a filter in front of it.

9
00:00:55,716 --> 00:01:04,467
The macula is visibly yellow, and that colour comes from three molecules: lutein, zeaxanthin, and meso zeaxanthin.

10
00:01:04,467 --> 00:01:09,591
Together they are called macular pigment, and they do two jobs.

11
00:01:09,591 --> 00:01:26,453
They absorb blue light before it reaches the photoreceptors underneath, taking the highest energy part of the visible range first. And they quench singlet oxygen, the exact damage that high light and high oxygen produce.

12
00:01:26,453 --> 00:01:41,327
Here is the part that matters. Your body cannot make any of them. Every molecule of pigment in your macula arrived there from something you ate. So what actually gets it there?

13
00:01:41,327 --> 00:01:48,372
This is where goji comes in. It is the richest known dietary source of zeaxanthin.

14
00:01:48,372 --> 00:01:56,343
But the interesting thing is not the amount, it is the form. In most plants zeaxanthin is free.

15
00:01:56,343 --> 00:02:06,376
In goji it is esterified. The molecule arrives with two palmitic acid chains attached, a form called zeaxanthin dipalmitate.

16
00:02:06,376 --> 00:02:16,979
It is already bonded to fat before it reaches you. That matters for absorption, and if you watched the last two videos you know why.

17
00:02:16,979 --> 00:02:23,242
Carotenoids are fat soluble. They need micelles, and micelles need fat.

18
00:02:23,242 --> 00:02:34,058
We said it with avocado, we said it again with tomato, and this is the third time. The fat is not the nutrient, the fat is the vehicle.

19
00:02:34,058 --> 00:02:37,047
Now follow it past the intestine.

20
00:02:37,047 --> 00:02:44,873
Carotenoids are packed into chylomicrons, enter the bloodstream, and transfer into your lipoproteins.

21
00:02:44,873 --> 00:02:47,649
Here the two stories separate.

22
00:02:47,649 --> 00:02:54,480
Lycopene concentrates in LDL particles, which is why it ends up inside the artery wall.

23
00:02:54,480 --> 00:03:01,311
Zeaxanthin and lutein travel mostly in HDL, and HDL takes them somewhere else entirely.

24
00:03:01,311 --> 00:03:04,798
They go to the eye, and not by accident.

25
00:03:04,798 --> 00:03:10,419
The retina carries a protein whose only job is to catch this molecule.

26
00:03:10,419 --> 00:03:20,096
It binds zeaxanthin selectively and pulls it into the tissue, and a second protein holds it in place so it does not drift away.

27
00:03:20,096 --> 00:03:25,930
Your eye has a dedicated receiving station for a molecule it cannot make.

28
00:03:25,930 --> 00:03:29,916
So does eating goji change anything measurable?

29
00:03:29,916 --> 00:03:40,305
This is the unusual part, because macular pigment can be measured directly. The number is called macular pigment optical density.

30
00:03:40,305 --> 00:03:57,025
In a randomised trial at the University of California, Davis, twenty seven adults aged forty five to sixty five were split into two groups for ninety days. One ate twenty eight grams of goji berries, five times a week.

31
00:03:57,025 --> 00:04:09,477
The other took a supplement with six milligrams of lutein and four milligrams of zeaxanthin. The berry group showed a significant increase in macular pigment.

32
00:04:09,477 --> 00:04:17,874
The supplement group showed no change at all. I want to be careful, because that is easy to oversell.

33
00:04:17,874 --> 00:04:32,960
It was a pilot study, twenty seven people, not blinded. And macular pigment optical density is a surrogate. It tells you the filter became denser, not that anyone kept their sight longer.

34
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:48,684
Large supplement trials have shown lutein and zeaxanthin can slow progression in people who already have age related macular degeneration. That is a different question, and this study does not replace it.

35
00:04:48,684 --> 00:05:06,331
But the comparison inside the trial is interesting, because it is the exact question we ended the tomato video on. Is it the whole food, or the single molecule? Here the whole food won and the isolated molecule did nothing.

36
00:05:06,331 --> 00:05:18,356
We do not know why. It could be the ester form, the fat that came with the berry, the other carotenoids beside it, or poor absorption of the supplement.

37
00:05:18,356 --> 00:05:21,274
One trial cannot separate those.

38
00:05:21,274 --> 00:05:32,235
So, four rules. One. About twenty eight grams a day, a small handful of dried berries. That is the dose that was studied.

39
00:05:32,235 --> 00:05:40,564
Two. Eat them with fat. No fat, no micelle, no delivery. Third time we have said it.

40
00:05:40,564 --> 00:05:47,398
Three. Whole berries, not an extract. That is what worked in the trial.

41
00:05:47,398 --> 00:05:55,085
Four. Think in months rather than weeks. The change was measured after ninety days.

42
00:05:55,085 --> 00:06:13,372
One warning that matters. Goji appears to affect a liver enzyme that clears certain drugs, and there are reported cases of altered clotting values in people taking warfarin. If you are on a blood thinner, speak to your doctor first.

43
00:06:13,372 --> 00:06:26,607
None of this was really about a berry. It was about a molecule your body cannot build, travelling to a place that is waiting for it, with a protein standing at the door.

44
00:06:26,607 --> 00:06:30,094
So which molecule should we follow next?

45
00:06:30,094 --> 00:06:36,640
Write a food and an organ in the comments, and we will take it apart, cell by cell.
